# Note about the TEST_TOKEN_8MIN
# The token in URLs containing TEST_TOKEN_8MIN is a placeholder representing an 8-minute test token. To make this work end-to-end you need a running proxy/auth server that:
#  - issues a token with 8-minute expiry to the client
#  - validates the token on /proxy/* requests and allows access only while token is valid
#  - optionally proxies the upstream HLS stream and enforces HTTPS/CORS/rate-limits
# See docs/STREAMING_ARCHITECTURE.md in the repo for an example server implementation and how to generate real tokens.
